      "side": 1,
      "message": "In much of the \"ordinary\" EC codebase, I would agree.  But this clock_set_osc() is called in early initialization, before the console UART is initialized, so there is not a lot of ways of getting an error message out.  You can see that line 210 in this file has a similar unbounded loop, waiting for hardware to finish setting up.  So I guess that if either the oscillator or voltage regulator is defective, of if there is a bug in the driver for either, we have to accept the possibility of not getting any meaningful output.",
